###
# DB-First Resolution Smoke Tests
# These tests verify that a credentialRef matching a vps.name is resolved from
# the database instead of the filesystem / S3.  They require the registered VPS
# names above to exist.  Real provider credentials are needed for a full
# round-trip; with placeholder tokens the session create will fail at the
# provider level (not at credential resolution), confirming DB lookup succeeded.

### 36. Create Codespaces Session Using DB VPS Name as credentialRef
# Expected: provider-level failure (invalid token) — NOT a credential-not-found
# error, which confirms DB resolution succeeded.
POST http://localhost:3200/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Server-Token: {{serverToken}}
X-Codespaces-Credentials: vm-manager-smoke

{
    "provider": "codespaces"
}

### 36.1. Create CodeSandbox Session Using DB VPS Name as credentialRef
# Same pattern — credential resolved from DB, provider rejects the placeholder token.
POST http://localhost:3200/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Server-Token: {{serverToken}}
X-CodeSandbox-Credentials: csb-smoke

{
    "provider": "codesandbox"
}

### 36.2. Create Codespaces Session Using Real VPS Name (live PAT)
# Replace vm-manager-smoke with a real registered name containing a valid PAT.
# @name createCodespacesSessionFromVps
POST http://localhost:3200/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Server-Token: {{serverToken}}
X-Codespaces-Credentials: {{codespacesCredentials}}

{
    "provider": "codespaces"
}

###
@codespacesVpsSessionId = {{createCodespacesSessionFromVps.response.body.$.id}}

### 36.3. Terminate Live VPS-Resolved Codespaces Session
DELETE http://localhost:3200/api/v1/sessions/{{codespacesVpsSessionId}}
X-Server-Token: {{serverToken}}

